<Project>
  <!--
    ShadowDusk.HLSL build-time check (issue #282): warn when the project resolves a Vortice.Dxc
    other than the one release ShadowDusk.HLSL runs with.

    Why it exists. ShadowDusk.HLSL depends on Vortice.Dxc [3.3.4] (an exact range): 3.3.4 ships
    ShadowDusk's pinned DXC natives (1.7.2212.40, e043f4a1) and ShadowDusk.HLSL is compiled
    against its managed API. Another package in the application (Evergine.DirectX12 pulls
    3.8.3, measured) or a direct / central-package-management reference can raise it. NuGet then
    warns NU1608 but still resolves the higher version, and every DirectX 12 / OpenGL / Vulkan
    compile fails at RUNTIME with SD0219 (3.8.3 is a different DXC, 1.9.2602.17, and a
    binary-incompatible API). This warning moves that discovery to build time and names the fix.

    A WARNING, never an error: DirectX 11 and FNA consumers do not use DXC and must keep
    building. Silence it with <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);SD0220</NoWarn> once the conflict is understood
    (measured: MSBuild honours NoWarn for it). Under TreatWarningsAsErrors the NU1608 that comes
    with the same graph already fails the restore.

    Shipped under buildTransitive/, so it runs for a project that references ShadowDusk.HLSL
    directly or through ShadowDusk.Compiler / ShadowDusk.ContentPipeline. The pin below must equal
    Directory.Packages.props and DxcNativeIdentity.PinnedVorticeDxcVersion (VorticeDxcPinTests).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <_ShadowDuskPinnedVorticeDxcVersion>3.3.4</_ShadowDuskPinnedVorticeDxcVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Target Name="_ShadowDuskCheckVorticeDxcVersion"
          AfterTargets="ResolvePackageAssets">
    <ItemGroup>
      <_ShadowDuskVorticeDxcAsset Include="@(ResolvedCompileFileDefinitions);@(RuntimeCopyLocalItems)"
                                  Condition="'%(NuGetPackageId)' == 'Vortice.Dxc'" />
      <_ShadowDuskVorticeDxcVersion Include="@(_ShadowDuskVorticeDxcAsset->'%(NuGetPackageVersion)'->Distinct())" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <PropertyGroup>
      <_ShadowDuskResolvedVorticeDxcVersion>@(_ShadowDuskVorticeDxcVersion)</_ShadowDuskResolvedVorticeDxcVersion>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <Warning Code="SD0220"
             Condition="'$(_ShadowDuskResolvedVorticeDxcVersion)' != '' and '$(_ShadowDuskResolvedVorticeDxcVersion)' != '$(_ShadowDuskPinnedVorticeDxcVersion)'"
             Text="This project resolves Vortice.Dxc $(_ShadowDuskResolvedVorticeDxcVersion), but ShadowDusk.HLSL runs only with Vortice.Dxc $(_ShadowDuskPinnedVorticeDxcVersion), the release that ships ShadowDusk's pinned DXC (1.7.2212.40). With any other version every DirectX 12, OpenGL and Vulkan compile fails at runtime with SD0219 (DirectX 11 and FNA do not use DXC and are unaffected). Fix: pin it in this project, &lt;PackageReference Include=&quot;Vortice.Dxc&quot; Version=&quot;$(_ShadowDuskPinnedVorticeDxcVersion)&quot; /&gt; (or the matching PackageVersion under central package management). If a package here requires the newer Vortice.Dxc (NU1608 above names it), ShadowDusk's DXC-backed targets cannot run in this application; compile those shaders at build time instead. Suppress with NoWarn SD0220." />
  </Target>
</Project>
